This section covers the foundational Docker tasks: building, running, managing, and troubleshooting containers. Each task has its own folder with the relevant files and notes.

📂 Task Overview
Task	Folder	Purpose	Key Files
Task 1 – Custom Nginx Container	nginx-container/	Build a custom Nginx image with your own index.html.	Dockerfile, index.html, notes.md
Task 2 – Deploy Official Nginx	deploy-nginx-container/	Run the official Nginx image directly.	notes.md
Task 3 – Delete Container	delete-container/	Stop and remove a running container.	notes.md
Task 4 – Copy File into Container	copy-file-container/	Copy files from host into a container.	notes.md
Task 5 – Troubleshoot Container	troubleshoot-container/	Diagnose issues with logs, inspect, restart, and exec.	notes.md


🚀 Workflow Summary
Verify Docker installation → docker --version, systemctl status docker

Build & run containers → docker build, docker run

Access services → test via http://localhost:8080

Manage lifecycle → docker stop, docker rm

Copy files → docker cp

Troubleshoot → docker logs, docker inspect, docker exec

✅ Learning Outcomes
Understand how to build custom images with Dockerfiles.

Deploy containers using official images.

Manage container lifecycle (start, stop, delete).

Copy files between host and container.

Troubleshoot containers effectively.
